###### Art.211.‐ Is punished by imprisonment from six months to five years and a fine of

1,000,000 to 10,000,000 FCFA, the act by anyone, of promising, offering or granting promises, gifts, presents or other undue advantages, without right, at any time, directly or indirectly, to a person who, without being a depositary of public authority, nor charged with a public service mission, nor invested with an elective public mandate, exercises, within the framework of a professional or social activity, a management function or work for a natural or legal person under public or private law or for any organization, for themselves or for another person, so that, in violation of their duties, they perform or refrain from performing an act.  
This penalty is accompanied by the complementary penalty of confiscation provided for in Article 28 of this Code.

###### Art.212

‐ Is punished by six months to five years imprisonment and a fine of 1,000,000 to 10,000,000 FCFA, the act by anyone who, without being a depositary of public authority nor charged with a public service mission, nor invested with an elective public mandate, exercises, within the framework of a professional or social activity, a management function or work for a natural or legal person under public or private law or for any organization, of soliciting or accepting, without right, at any time, directly or indirectly, offers or promises or receiving gifts or presents or other undue advantages for themselves or for another person, in order to perform or refrain from performing an act in violation of their duties.  
This penalty is accompanied by the complementary penalty of confiscation provided for in Article 28 of this Code.

##### Chapitre 8 ‐ Aggravated fraud

###### Art.213

‐ Is punished by imprisonment from three to ten years and a fine equal to triple the value at stake, anyone who commits the offense of fraud when it is carried out:
• 1) by a person who is a depositary of public authority or charged with a public service mission in the exercise or on the occasion of the exercise of their functions;  
• 2) by a person who unduly assumes the capacity of a person who is a depositary of public authority or charged with a public service mission;  
• 3) by a person having made an appeal to the public with a view to the issuance of shares, bonds, vouchers, units or any securities whatsoever of either a company or a commercial or industrial enterprise;  
50

• 4) to the detriment of a person whose particular vulnerability, due to their age, an illness, an infirmity, a physical or mental deficiency or a state of pregnancy, is apparent or known to its perpetrator;  
• 5) in an organized gang, that is to say by a grouping formed or an understanding established for this purpose.

###### Art.214

‐ Is punished by imprisonment from one to five years and a fine whose maximum rate is equal to triple the value at stake, anyone who commits the offense of fraud provided for in Article 213 of this Code when the fraud is based on a permanent race between the collection of new funds and payments aimed at giving confidence.  
When this fraud relates to an appeal to public savings, it is punished by imprisonment from five to ten years and a fine equal to triple the amount extorted.  
This penalty is accompanied by the complementary penalty of confiscation provided for in Article 28 of this Code.

##### Chapitre 9 ‐ Corruption in relation to public procurement Art.215.‐ Is

punished by imprisonment from one to ten years and a fine of 500,000 to 10,000,000 FCFA, any person who, by non-observance of the rules for awarding, executing and monitoring public procurement, obtains or causes a third party to obtain, directly or indirectly, an undue advantage.

###### Art.216

‐ Also constitute acts of corruption in relation to public procurement and are punished in accordance with the provisions of Article 215 above:
• a) the award of a contract to a service provider without legal existence;  
• b) the award of a contract with a company in financial distress, with third parties or companies in the suspect period of bankruptcy or judicial liquidation;  
• c) the award of a contract with a company not presenting sufficient financial, economic and technical guarantees.

###### Art.217

‐ Constitute systematic negligence in relation to public procurement and are punished in accordance with the provisions of Article 215 above:
• a) the non-transmission, in a repeated manner, of files to members of the Procurement Commissions within the regulatory deadlines and forms;  
• b) the non-convening, in a repeated manner, of the independent observer for contracts falling within their competence;  
• c) the convening in disregard of deadline rules having the purpose or consequence of delaying the presence or causing the absence of members of the Commissions and the independent observer;  
• d) the non-transmission, in a repeated manner, of documents to the body in charge of regularization of contracts within the regulatory deadlines;  
• e) the non-termination of the contract in cases of termination by operation of law;  
51

• f) the non-transmission of termination acts to the body in charge of regularization of public procurement;  
• g) the non-payment of regulatory fees;  
• h) the non-transmission of documents relating to the execution of contracts to the body in charge of regulation of public procurement.

###### Art.218

‐ Constitute a refusal of service due in relation to public procurement and are punished in accordance with the provisions of Article 215 above:
• a) the refusal to sell the tender file or the concealment of the tender file;  
• b) the refusal to communicate to a tenderer, after their request, the documents to which they are entitled;  
• c) unjustified delays in payments;  
• d) the non-execution of prescriptions granted within the framework of pledging;  
• e) the unjustified refusal of visa;  
• f) the non-compliance with deadlines for approval of statements;  
• g) the unjustified refusal to release securities or to issue the corresponding releases within the prescribed deadlines.

###### Art.219

‐ Constitute forgery in public and authentic writings in relation to public procurement and are punished in accordance with the provisions of Article 215 above:
• a) the change of contract stipulations without a related amendment duly adopted;  
• b) the modification of the content of the final text of the draft contract in relation to the data of the tender file.

###### Art.220

‐ Constitutes forgery in private or commercial writing in relation to public procurement and is punished in accordance with the provisions of Article 215 above, the provision of false documents in the tender file.

###### Art.221

‐ Constitute extortion in relation to public procurement and are punished in accordance with the provisions of Article 215 above:
• a) the non-application of delay penalties;  
• b) the lifting of penalties without prior authorization from the body in charge of regulation of the public procurement sector;  
• c) the retention, without any valid reason, of a file.

###### Art.222

‐ Constitute favoritism in relation to public procurement and are punished in accordance with the provisions of Article 215 above:
• a) the communication in advance to a tenderer of information on the call for tenders with the aim of favoring them in relation to their competitors;  
• b) the receipt of offers after the deadline;  
• c) the steering of an evaluation.  
52

#### Title 6 ‐ Piracy

##### Chapter 1 ‐ Unlawful acts against civil aviation

###### Art.280

‐ Any person who commits an act contrary to the provisions of civil aviation regulations and of a nature to endanger or endangering the safety of an aircraft in flight or on the ground, persons or property on board, is guilty of an unlawful act against the safety of civil aviation and is punished by life imprisonment.  
63

Any person who commits any of the following acts is also guilty of an unlawful act against the safety of civil aviation and punished by life imprisonment:
• a) seizes by violence or threat of violence an aircraft in flight, in service or out of service, or exercises control over it;  
• b) destroys or seriously damages installations of a national or international airport serving civil aviation;  
• c) impairs or disrupts air navigation services;  
• d) destroys or seriously damages aircraft parked at a Chadian airport or in service;  
• e) makes threats of any kind or commits acts of unlawful interference directed against passengers, crews, ground personnel or the public;  
• f) commits against a person or property, in an airport, an act of violence which causes or is likely to cause serious injury or death to that person or destruction of that property, or if that act endangers or is likely to endanger safety in that airport;  
• g) destroys or damages air navigation aids;  
• h) communicates false information likely to endanger the safety of an aircraft in flight;  
• i) introduces or participates in the introduction on board an aircraft of devices or substances likely to destroy or damage the aircraft or endanger the flight;  
• j) uses an aircraft in service for the purpose of causing death, or causing serious bodily injury or serious damage to property or the environment;  
• k) manufactures or transports unmarked explosives, except where they are authorized military devices within the meaning of the Convention on the Marking of Plastic Explosives for the Purpose of Detection.  
Any person who, using a device, substance or weapon, commits any of the following acts is also guilty of an unlawful act against the safety of civil aviation and punished by life imprisonment:
• a) commits against a person, in an airport serving national or international civil aviation, an act of violence which causes or is likely to cause serious injury or death;  
• b) destroys or seriously damages the installations of an airport serving national or international civil aviation or aircraft not in service located in the airport, or disrupts the services of the airport, if that act endangers or is likely to endanger safety in that airport.

##### Chapter 2

‐ Unlawful acts against maritime navigation and fixed platforms

###### Art.281

‐ Any person who commits an act contrary to the provisions of regulations relating to the safety of maritime navigation of a nature to endanger or endangering the safety of a ship at sea or in a port, persons or property on board, or good order and discipline on board, is guilty of an offence against the safety of maritime navigation and is punished by life imprisonment.  
64

Any person who unlawfully commits any of the following acts is also guilty of an offence against the safety of maritime navigation and punished by life imprisonment:
• a) seizes by violence or threat of violence a ship under way, in service or out of service, or exercises control over it;  
• b) destroys or seriously damages installations of a national or international port serving maritime navigation;  
• c) destroys or seriously damages ships stationed in a port or in service;  
• d) makes threats of any kind or commits acts of unlawful interference directed against passengers, crews, ground personnel or the public;  
• e) commits against a person or property in a port, an act of violence which causes or is likely to cause serious injury or death to that person or destruction of that property, if that act endangers or is likely to endanger safety in that port;  
• f) destroys or damages maritime navigation aids;  
• g) communicates false information likely to endanger the safety of navigation of a ship;  
• h) introduces or participates in the introduction on board a ship of devices or substances likely to destroy or damage the ship or its cargo or endanger the navigation of the ship;  
• i) manufactures or transports unmarked explosives, except where they are authorized military devices within the meaning of the Convention on the Marking of Plastic Explosives for the Purpose of Detection.

###### Art.282

‐ Any person who commits any of the following acts is guilty of an offence against the safety of fixed platforms and is punished by life imprisonment:
• a) seizes a platform or exercises control over it, by violence or threat of violence;  
• b) destroys a platform or causes damage to it likely to endanger its safety;  
• c) commits an act of violence against a person on board a platform, if that act is likely to endanger the safety of the platform;  
• d) places or causes to be placed on a platform, by any means whatsoever, a device or substance capable of destroying the platform or likely to endanger its safety;  
• e) causes injury or death to a person, where such acts are connected with offences provided for in points a, b, c and d above.

###### Art.283

‐ Any person who commits any of the following acts is guilty of an offence against the safety of fixed platforms and is punished by life imprisonment:
• a) uses against or on board a ship or fixed platform, or discharges from a ship or fixed platform, radioactive materials, explosives or BCN weapons, in a manner that causes or is likely to cause death or serious damage;  
65

• b) discharges, from a ship or fixed platform, hydrocarbons, liquefied natural gas, or other harmful or potentially dangerous substances, not covered by paragraph a), in such quantity or concentration as causes or is likely to cause serious bodily or material damage;  
• c) uses a ship in a manner that causes death or serious bodily or material damage;  
• d) commits an act which, by its nature or context, is intended to intimidate a population or to compel a Government, an international or intergovernmental organization to do or abstain from doing any act.  
Any person who threatens to commit one of the offences provided for in paragraph 1 is punished by the same penalty.

###### Art.284

‐ Public prosecution for offences provided for in this title is not subject to any statute of limitations.

